    <item>
      <title>0.8.9</title>
      <pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 20:15:00 +0300</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>26</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8.9</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <ul>
          <li>History: a new sidebar section keeps a private record of what you played — top artists, top tracks, a recent feed, Clear history. The log stays in a file on your Mac.</li>
          <li>DAC dossier: Settings → Audio asks your DAC what it can actually do — sample rates, bit depths, DoP ceiling, hardware volume — and can test exclusive access live.</li>
          <li>Signal path receipt: the signal-path popover copies or saves a plain-text report of everything between the file and the DAC, fingerprinted with SHA-256.</li>
          <li>Network panel: Settings → Network lists every outgoing request — host, reason, outcome, size.</li>
          <li>Automatic updates: Rubis checks at launch and can install a new version on quit. Settings → General → Updates.</li>
          <li>Playback errors now say what happened in words, including a device that refuses a sample rate.</li>
          <li>Layout: Now Playing stays readable in a small window, Albums sizes the showcase to the window, Tracks hides columns instead of truncating them.</li>
        </ul>
      ]]></description>
