      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <ul>
          <li>Now Playing shows the queue and the liner notes at once: cover and queue on top, notes as a wide band below.</li>
          <li>Liner notes are written by your chosen writer first (Claude or DeepSeek); Wikipedia steps in when there is no key or the album is unknown.</li>
          <li>Wikipedia finds far more records — the old lookup only matched article titles, so most albums came back empty.</li>
          <li>The album shelf, the queue and the notes share one scroll indicator: a gold thumb in a ruby setting, and you can drag it.</li>
          <li>Fixed: the keychain password dialog kept returning because reading a key rewrote it and threw away your “Always Allow”.</li>
        </ul>
      ]]></description>
